    "body": "## Goal\n\nFirst G4 product feature: update **an existing** VanDesign base cabinet from a revised specification, preserving its managed assembly and detecting conflicts before mutation. This is not merely editing a Fusion parameter manually.\n\n## Implemented\n\n- `preview_width_change`: read-only proposed width change, affected parameters/panels/cuts, new canonical hash and refusal reasons.\n- `update_width`: preflight validation and drift detection, write-ahead restore journal, in-place Fusion parameter update, saved-spec/hash update via G3 adapter, geometry and managed-ID validation, rollback on failure.\n- Negative handling for out-of-range widths, manual parameter drift and uncertain restoration.\n- Regression fixes for job-state file locking, add-in restart module caching and rollback count checks.\n- Focused offline tests and example job; documentation in `automation/G4_WIDTH_UPDATE.md`.\n\n## Claude-reported real-Fusion demonstration (independent original evidence review pending)\n\n- Fusion 2705.1.30, separate test design `v5-g4-width-demo`.\n- `1200 → 1100 mm`: **7/7 automated steps PASS**, approximately **0.77 seconds** for the batch.\n- 59/59 validation checks before and after; shelf 1175.4 → 1075.4 mm; doors 595.5 → 545.5 mm.\n- Spec SHA changed from `0db0be53…` to `8788ca17…`; 8 stable managed IDs preserved, 28 timeline items unchanged; targeted cut audit 2/2 PASS.\n- Rejected 30 mm width proposal; refused update after deliberate conflicting dado edit (restored safely).\n- Claude reports save, close and reopen produced 59/59, cut audit 2/2 and unchanged identity/hashes.\n- **54 offline tests reported PASS**.\n- Local evidence: `G4-width-update-evidence-20261015.zip` (62 files, SHA-256 reported beginning `a409215f`). The local ZIP has not yet been independently uploaded/reviewed here.\n\n## Scope limits\n\n- Width-only in-place update of one cabinet; base@1 is the demonstrated fixture.\n- No shelf/door structural count changes, furniture placement or UI.\n- Runner does not save designs; the save/reopen check required a manual Fusion action.\n- Fusion Personal editable-document limit remains an environmental constraint.\n- No manufacturing or CAM qualification.\n\n## Dependency / merge safety\n\n**Base:** `feature/fusion-automation-runner` (draft PR #6), because this feature depends on its queue, commands, Fusion add-in and G3 adapter. PR #6 itself depends on G3 draft PR #5. This is a **stacked draft PR**; do not retarget to `main`, merge or close the earlier PRs without a reviewed integration plan.\n\n## Review criteria\n\nReview the actual ZIP evidence, CI, no-mutation refusal and rollback behavior, correct canonical spec/hash readback, identity/timeline preservation and safe save/reopen. Accept only the scope actually tested.\n\n**Next product focus after acceptance:** start a visible, simplified campervan interior assembly with a bed, kitchen furniture and existing cabinet modules, reusing the verified geometry framework.",
