        "body": "## Independent real-Fusion evidence review — G4 width update (2026-10-15)\n\n**ACCEPTED for the demonstrated, narrow G4 base-cabinet width-update scope.** Independently inspected the actual user-uploaded archive `G4-width-update-evidence-20261015.zip` (SHA-256 `a409215f11543f65e512c4106b47f8ff7cb78e656b79cd44432edfcc86d11a74`). Its **62 manifest-listed evidence files** all matched their declared SHA-256 and byte sizes; ZIP has 63 entries including the manifest.\n\n**Successful real-Fusion batch**: `g4-demo-width-1100` outcome PASS; 7/7 steps passed in 773.6 ms inside Fusion 2705.1.30; before width1200 / shelf1175.4 / door widths595.5, after width1100 / shelf1075.4 / door widths545.5. Both before/after measurements have **59 unique named checks PASS**, zero FAIL/UNKNOWN. All eight original stable managed IDs occur exactly once before, after and in post-reopen inspection. Counts unchanged: 16 user params, 8 root occurrences, 9 components, 28 timeline items. Both schema0.2 canonical spec hashes independently recomputed: `0db0be535621b56469735b052624d0f071300aacf7b4b5efbfa0d663edee905c` to `8788ca176d56ff815c734d5aa4a658fcb5fcf13f2767b1deb3bfb690f7acb8d2`, and stored hash readback matches.\n\n**Independent cut audits:** Both post-update and post-reopen original TXT+JSON output report 2/2 correct targeted cut operations, each with exactly one participant body (corresponding side panel, never shelf), `timeline_restored=true`, before/after counts equal, overall PASS.\n\n**Persistence evidence:** Post-reopen inspect is same Fusion cloud design identity, version 3, `is_modified:false`, correct new stored hash and managed IDs; original remeasure is 59/59 PASS and its full parameter records, entire validation records and design-spec canonical JSON are exactly equal to the post-update measurement. UI close/reopen action itself is Claude-reported; post-reopen Fusion data independently corroborates persistent version.\n\n**Expected negative tests:** 30mm preview refused both configured bounds and G3 `width_fits`. After deliberate dado drift (6→10mm), `update_width` refused with four named discrepancies, did not apply width update, and original 6mm was restored with 59/59 validation. Earlier pre-restart probes returned schema `unknown command`; the successful post-restart probes verify the corrected installation. No unexpected validation failures in positive checks.\n\n**Limits:** This is evidence acceptance for one existing base@1 cabinet and width-only update, **not** general G4 structural regeneration, other furniture, arbitrary manual-feature conflicts, CAM or manufacturing approval. Runner doesn't auto-save; one human save/reopen is covered. No comprehensive code security audit conducted here. Keep stacked PR #7 draft, dependent on runner PR #6 and G3 PR #5. Prioritise visible simplified campervan-interior demonstration next rather than expanding infrastructure.",
